.TH "RAPTOR-ANALYTIC" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-analytic \- Solve the static subset of an RBD exactly: series, parallel, mixed, k\-out\-of\-n and hierarchies. Reliability mode is non\-repairable. Availability mode is steady state, independent components, perfect repair. Models outside that subset are refused with the first offending element.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor analytic\fR [\-h] [\-\-mode {reliability,availability,both}] [\-\-hierarchy NAME|ID] [\-\-at T] [\-\-times T1,T2,...] [\-\-bx X1,X2,...] [\-\-tau T] [\-\-importance] [\-\-no\-importance] [\-\-equation] [\-\-ignore\-repairs] [\-\-ignore LIST] [\-\-phase N|all] [\-\-standby {active,absent}] [\-\-dependencies {up,down}] [\-\-max\-variables N] [\-\-max\-bdd\-nodes N] [\-\-progress {auto,bar,json,none}] [\-\-xlsx PATH] [\-f {text,json,csv}] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Solve the static subset of an RBD exactly: series, parallel, mixed, k\-out\-of\-n and hierarchies. Reliability mode is non\-repairable. Availability mode is steady state, independent components, perfect repair. Models outside that subset are refused with the first offending element.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI{reliability|availability|both}\fR
reliability (R(t), non\-repairable), availability (steady state, repairable), or both with the same settings (default reliability)
.TP
\fB\-\-hierarchy\fR \fINAME|ID\fR
analyse one hierarchy as a standalone model; its In node becomes Start and its Out node End
.TP
\fB\-\-at\fR \fIT\fR
mission time for reliability mode (default: the model's run length); ignored in availability mode
.TP
\fB\-\-times\fR \fIT1,T2,...\fR
also evaluate a curve at these times
.TP
\fB\-\-bx\fR \fIX1,X2,...\fR
BX life percentages for reliability mode (default 10); ignored in availability mode
.TP
\fB\-\-tau\fR \fIT\fR
conditional reliability for another mission of T after \-\-at
.TP
\fB\-\-importance\fR
exact Birnbaum/RAW/RRW/VF/criticality (default on)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-importance\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-equation\fR
print the path\-product equation
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-repairs\fR
reliability mode only: compute first\-failure reliability even when the model has repair distributions
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\fR \fILIST\fR
comma\-separated simulation\-only features to leave out instead of refusing: repairs (reliability mode), pm, spares, resources
.TP
\fB\-\-phase\fR \fIN|all\fR
analyse a phased model as if it stayed in phase N (1\-based) the whole time; all solves each phase on its own, one result per phase
.TP
\fB\-\-standby\fR \fI{active|absent}\fR
cold\-standby paths: treat as fully in service, or as if they did not exist
.TP
\fB\-\-dependencies\fR \fI{up|down}\fR
treat every dependency as up (analyse the dependent element's own law) or down (remove it from the success path)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-variables\fR \fIN\fR
raise the BDD variable limit (default: solver setting) when a large model is still tractable
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-bdd\-nodes\fR \fIN\fR
raise the BDD node limit (default 2,000,000, about 0.7 GB); at most half of the free memory at 350 bytes a node
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI{auto|bar|json|none}\fR
progress on stderr: one percentage for the whole solve (building the diagram, then the results), with the stage and the time left (auto = bar only on a terminal)
.TP
\fB\-\-xlsx\fR \fIPATH\fR
also write the result as a spreadsheet (one set of sheets per mode and phase with \-\-mode both or \-\-phase all); a folder gets the default name, e.g. MODEL_analytical_reliability.xlsx
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json|csv}\fR
stdout format; with several results (\-\-mode both, \-\-phase all) json is {"results": [...]} and csv has mode and phase columns
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Exact reliability at one year, with MTTF, B10 life and importance.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor analytic plant.rbds \-\-at 8760\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reliability and availability with the same settings, both in one workbook, out/plant_analytical_reliability_availability.xlsx.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor analytic plant.rbds \-\-mode both \-\-ignore repairs,pm \-\-xlsx out/\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
One hierarchy on its own; progress as JSON events on stderr, the result as JSON on stdout.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor analytic plant.rbds \-\-hierarchy Cooling \-\-progress json \-f json\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
